laurel 2786: cellular: the radio can go online after IPA on, and iOS gets a state to read. DMS GET_OPERATING_MODE every 10 s until online, 60 s after that (boot 20:02: one read at ~450 ms said 5 "shutting down" and blocked ONLINE for the boot); no first line while the modem says 4, 5 or no mode (60 s limit). SET_OPERATING_MODE online: 6 tries, the line says when the modem refuses. NAS BIND_SUBSCRIPTION: 6 tries, 10 s apart (boot 20:02: error 3 while UIM starts, never asked again, so nas2 would read the primary subscription); nas2 without a binding reports no registration. A NAS error clears the old registration and signal. Line prefix: "on" only with the radio online, else "part" (half-done-audit row 3), and it says data, SMS and voice are off. New sysctls: kern.laurel_cell_state (key=value, written by the watch thread: bars 0-4 from the kernel's own reading, only when registered; never ICCID, IMSI, IMEI), kern.laurel_cell_ui (the SpringBoard bridge's result line for the USB log, at most 16 lines a boot). Details: docs/laurel_sprout/cellular.md section 9.

